Not applied by default. Written while debugging a Zero 3E that turned out to have
defective Ethernet hardware, so neither is verified on a good board:

- board-radxa-zero-3e-ethernet-phy-reset.patch: PHY reset on the MDIO bus. Only needed
  if the bootloader leaves the PHY in reset ("cannot attach to PHY (error: -ENODEV)"),
  e.g. with U-Boot newer than the board's pinned v2025.10.
- general-rtl8211f-disable-aldps-when-mac-needs-rxc.patch: force RTL8211F ALDPS off.

To use one, copy it to userpatches/kernel/rockchip64/.
